Rule 5 (index tensor and input tensor must have same shape except for the dimension dim)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : if i ≠ v_2 then shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_3, i)
>>
Rule 6 (If dim is negative, it should be translated to a positive dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 < 0 then v_2 + ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 7 (output tensor has the same shape as index tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
